{{ macros.section(3, "Pragma Protocol", id="pragma-protocol") }}

{{ macros.protocol('__pragma__',
    capability='Resolved pragma settings; a type of program-manifest.',
    surface='Read a setting via `__pragma__.get` / `.append` / `.sh`. `${__pragma__}` is the whole JSON manifest and a same-name observer target.',
    notes='The compile-time twin of the `CMK_PRAGMA_*` env namespace, and the pragma member of the program self-model triad (`__plugins__` / `__modules__` / `__pragma__`).',
    mkdocs=mkdocs) }}

Nothing outside the compiler touches the `CMK_PRAGMA_*` wire-format directly; consumers read settings through the `__pragma__` resolvers instead:

| resolver | reads | semantics |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `__pragma__.get(<name>, <default>)` | one scalar key | *replace* (pragma > env > default, warns on override) |
| `__pragma__.append(<name>, <default>)` | one list key | *accumulate* (env and pragma both contribute, like `+=`) |
| `__pragma__.sh(<KEY>)` | shell-time reader | a `sed` filter over the compiled `export CMK_PRAGMA_*` lines, for boot/compile stages where make is not yet up |
| `${__pragma__}` | the whole manifest | one compact JSON object (e.g. `{"recipe_join":";","vm_trace":"1"}`); lazy `$(shell …)`, degrades to `{}` when empty |

The `__pragma__` self-model is also an observer target that prints the manifest.  Like the rest of the [program self-model triad]({{_}}/plugins/overview#program-self-models), it is queryable as both a variable and a same-name target.

<br/>

{{ macros.section(3, "Catalog", id="catalog") }}

Every shipped pragma at a glance; click a key for the full description [below](#reference).  The *(boot)* pragmas configure a program's lifecycle rather than its compilation; they take effect only via `cmk run` and are detailed with the [supervisor machinery]({{_}}/runtime/#lifecycle-boot-settings).

| Pragma | Syntax | What it does | Used by |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [`recipe_join`](#pragma-recipe_join) | `"recipe_join": "&&"` \| `";"` \| `"none"` | Connector joining recipe-body lines: fail-fast / run-all / classic per-line. | - |
| [`plugin_pragma_allowed`](#pragma-plugin_pragma_allowed) | `"plugin_pragma_allowed": true` | Two-pass compile: let imported plugins' pragma alter the importer. | - |
| [`compiler_pre`](#pragma-compiler_pre_post) / [`compiler_post`](#pragma-compiler_pre_post) | `"compiler_pre": ["stage"]` | Splice extra preprocessor stages before / after the core chain. | {{macros.repo_link('demos/cmk/vm-coroutines.cmk', name='vm-coroutines.cmk', github=github)}} |
| [`vm_hydrate`](#pragma-compiler_pre_post) | `"vm_hydrate": true` | Alias for `compiler_pre += vm_hydrate` (auto-load the VM stage). | [`virtual-machine`]({{_}}/modules/virtual-machine) |
| [`target_locals`](#pragma-target_locals) | `"target_locals": true` | Enable per-recipe `__locals__()` capture (the vars a recipe defined). | {{macros.repo_link('demos/cmk/jqd.cmk', name='jqd.cmk', github=github)}} |
| [`bootloaders`](#pragma-lifecycle) | `"bootloaders": ["name"]` | *(boot)* Bash `define`s sourced in the supervisor before make. | {{macros.repo_link('demos/cmk/pragma-boot.cmk', name='pragma-boot.cmk', github=github)}} |
| [`cmk_pre`](#pragma-lifecycle) / [`cmk_post`](#pragma-lifecycle) | `"cmk_pre": ["target"]` | *(boot)* Make targets run before / after the main pipeline. | {{macros.repo_link('demos/cmk/pragma-boot.cmk', name='pragma-boot.cmk', github=github)}} |
| [`hooks`](#pragma-lifecycle) | `"hooks": "off"` | *(boot)* Disable `<target>.pre` / `.post` target-rewriting. | - |
| [`bootloader_disabled`](#pragma-lifecycle) | `"bootloader_disabled": true` | *(boot)* Skip the bootloader entirely. | - |

The interactive [`repl`](#repl) pragma (how a program *runs*, rather than how it compiles or boots) has its own [section below](#repl).

